2. Player2 Key Restriction (Revenue / Attribution Protection)

The Software includes functionality to interface with the Player2 platform/API.
To do so, it contains an embedded application credential / developer attribution
identifier (the "Player2 Game Key"), stored in obfuscated form in:

  - src/security.ts (the embedded encoded array named "_enc")

If you distribute (including publish, provide downloads, sell, or otherwise make
available) any version of the Software that connects to, interfaces with, or
utilizes the Player2 platform/API, you may NOT alter, replace, remove, or bypass
the embedded Player2 Game Key in src/security.ts, nor distribute a version
configured to use a different Player2 developer key for Player2 connectivity.

This restriction is intended to prevent republishing on the Player2 platform
in a way that redirects Player2 revenue/attribution away from the original
developer of P2 Claw.

